{"id": "EUVD-2026-82032", "enisaUuid": "883ac0df-74d7-33a6-85ec-a5ef1a0d439a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: fix RXDMAD_C buffer recycling race\n\nThe RXDMAD_C buffers come from the RRO data queues' page pools, which are\nbound to a different NAPI, so the direct page-pool recycle used here could\nrace the owning NAPI; take the non-direct path as is already done for WED\nRX queues.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:30", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ac05ed3a50e511c93f8506e555709a208dfce0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a273dc3b86a7d983d643827d3d3c795d55d8f632", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1f97c10a4ec2b9db69a134b757304399ca903ce"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hm23-4fh6-jvgr", "CVE-2026-90371"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "207128f0-bcf5-3bfe-bf0f-f5472c38dd0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e50d4d710efd2dbc46965e9608bbb502bcfc5c99 <e1f97c10a4ec2b9db69a134b757304399ca903ce"}, {"id": "228d957b-1066-3b44-9381-da28469619a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e50d4d710efd2dbc46965e9608bbb502bcfc5c99 <7ac05ed3a50e511c93f8506e555709a208dfce0a"}, {"id": "52623811-9157-36f7-9377-01b007479b93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "9d7f6536-7b8c-36e1-8c06-ff93ae40a8e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ad01512c-04cc-301d-b500-773047138b5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e50d4d710efd2dbc46965e9608bbb502bcfc5c99 <a273dc3b86a7d983d643827d3d3c795d55d8f632"}, {"id": "e75008e8-8355-354a-b7f9-afb0e0c8395f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor":